From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:09:20 +0300
Subject: main: close the audio and SDL before exiting

main() returned after gfx_shutdown() without snd_shutdown() or SDL_Quit(),
so SDL_mixer's audio thread was still running while exit() ran the
libraries' destructors. With SDL 1.2 provided by sdl12-compat (over SDL2 and
SDL3, as in Debian now) the thread then called into torn-down state and the
game segfaulted on every quit, from the menu or on SIGTERM.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -77,7 +77,11 @@ main (int argc, char **argv)
 		}
 	}
 
+    /* close the audio before exit: the mixer's thread kept running into exit()'s destructors
+     * and crashed there (sdl12-compat over SDL2/SDL3) */
+    snd_shutdown ();
     gfx_shutdown ();
+    SDL_Quit ();
 
     return 0;
 };
